7592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429405 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429406 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429407 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429408 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429409 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1031 "Describing Planar Regions Using Set-Builder Notation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1033 4392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1034 0.7710171825637773 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051063 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7df685b7-b3c7-5f49-ba38-fa8edde1bc9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186128540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186128541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186128542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186128543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186128544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128539 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128539 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128539 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1b810ea7-b064-5fb2-907f-f94838c98873" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128540 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128540 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128540 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "907234f6-d41d-59c4-b707-3a4bc0a94e07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128541 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128541 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128541 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9ed8dda-c357-5308-97b6-a92c738ce5dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128542 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128542 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128542 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f9741cfe-9a2e-51ba-9f5d-1bbc05258f58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128543 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128543 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128543 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b435149-51ff-523f-b255-3bdd5a506e85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128544 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128544 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128544 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "704224b1-5570-5b35-8983-4889e11c0891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128983 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6097" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128983 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}  \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x  \\, \\textrm{d}y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128983 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5110af12-1d0a-5f7e-8a3b-626cc437c53e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128983 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128984 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6098" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128984 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where \n$D=\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128984 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bd93891e-1f9f-51af-a5c2-4eb5ca1178d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128984 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-\\frac{y}{x}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4}-(-\\frac{y}{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128985 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6099" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128985 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.$\n\nI. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n\nII. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{2}  \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\,  \\text{d}x$\n\nIII. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128985 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e51c2aa9-027b-5b23-bcaf-805804a8de9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128985 #edb/ref 1074 "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  \n= \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x} .\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186235541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362508 #ed